(6) Tj T*
(Introduction) Tj T*
(For most of computing history, programming has been an act of translation: understand) Tj T*
(the problem in human terms, design a solution in abstract terms, then render it in syntax a) Tj T*
(machine can execute. Each step introduces friction. That friction is now collapsing. Software) Tj T*
(engineering is undergoing its most significant transformation since the introduction of) Tj T*
(The most profound shift in) Tj T*
(software engineering isn't a new) Tj T*
(language, framework, or cloud) Tj T*
(service. It's the transition from) Tj T*
(writing code to expressing intent,) Tj T*
(and trusting intelligent systems to) Tj T*
(translate that intent into working) Tj T*
(software.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
