(7) Tj T*
(high-level programming languages. For decades, the developer's primary interface with) Tj T*
(the machine has been syntax: curly braces, semicolons, type annotations, and the precise) Tj T*
(grammar of programming languages. That era is ending.) Tj T*
(A new paradigm has arrived in which developers express what they want to build rather) Tj T*
(than how to build it. The machine handles implementation. The human provides intent,) Tj T*
(architecture, and judgment. This isn't a distant future - it's the daily reality for a rapidly) Tj T*
(growing number of professional developers. As of early 2026, 85% of professional developers) Tj T*
(regularly use AI Coding Agents, 51% use them daily, and an estimated 41% of all new code) Tj T*
(is AI-generated.1) Tj T*
(This shift didn't happen overnight. It began with autocomplete - simple token prediction in) Tj T*
(the editor. Then came inline code suggestions that could complete entire functions. Next,) Tj T*
(chat-based interfaces allowed developers to describe features in natural language and) Tj T*
(receive working implementations. Now, fully autonomous agents can clone repositories,) Tj T*
(plan multi-file changes, execute them in sandboxed environments, run tests, and submit pull) Tj T*
(requests - all without a human typing a single line of code.) Tj T*
ET
