(This paper provides the foundation for that conversation. We trace the spectrum from casual) Tj T*
(vibe coding to disciplined agentic engineering, examine how the developer's role is shifting) Tj T*
(from writing code to exercising judgment -- from conductor to orchestrator -- and lay out) Tj T*
(what it takes to adopt these tools in ways that produce software you can actually depend on.) Tj T*
(Why this paper, why now) Tj T*
(New tools, capabilities, and paradigms emerge weekly. Engineering teams need a framework) Tj T*
(for making sense of this landscape - not a snapshot that will be outdated in months, but a set) Tj T*
(of principles and mental models that will remain useful as the specific tools evolve.) Tj T*
(Who this paper is for) Tj T*
(This paper is for software engineers, engineering managers, architects, and technical) Tj T*
(leaders who want to understand how AI is reshaping the SDLC and adopt these new) Tj T*
(capabilities without sacrificing the discipline that production software demands. We assume) Tj T*
(familiarity with modern software development practices but not with the specifics of AI or) Tj T*
(machine learning.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
