(Page 15 of 51 - 02 - The New SDLC  With Vibe Coding) Tj T*
(The new SDLC with vibe coding) Tj T*
(May 2026) Tj T*
(15) Tj T*
(parts that are not deterministic: did the agent take the right trajectory of steps, choose the) Tj T*
(right tools, and produce a final response that meets the quality bar. Tests are checked by) Tj T*
(code; evals are checked by labelled datasets, scoring rubrics, and LM judges. Without both,) Tj T*
(the practice is always vibe coding, regardless of how sophisticated the prompts are.) Tj T*
(Context engineering: the real skill) Tj T*
(As the field has matured, a key insight has emerged: the quality of AI-generated code) Tj T*
(depends less on the cleverness of your prompts and more on the quality of the context) Tj T*
(provided. This realization has given rise to the concept of context engineering, the practice) Tj T*
(of providing AI agents with rich, structured information about your codebase, architecture,) Tj T*
(conventions, and intent.5) Tj T*
(Developers must consider six primary types of context:) Tj T*
(* Instructions: The agent's core role, goals, and operational boundaries.) Tj T*
(* Knowledge: Retrieved documents, architectural diagrams, and domain-specific data.) Tj T*
(* Memory: Short-term session logs \(what just happened\) and long-term persistent state) Tj T*
(\(what the project is\).) Tj T*
(* Examples: Few-shot behavioral demonstrations and codebase reference patterns.) Tj T*
(* Tools: The precise definitions of the APIs, scripts, and external services the agent) Tj T*
(can invoke.) Tj T*
(* Guardrails: Hard constraints, formatting rules, and safety validations.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
