(Page 16 of 51 - 02 - The New SDLC  With Vibe Coding) Tj T*
(The new SDLC with vibe coding) Tj T*
(May 2026) Tj T*
(16) Tj T*
(In AI code generation, context engineering involves carefully balancing which of these six) Tj T*
(elements the agent possesses upfront versus what it can retrieve on demand. This creates a) Tj T*
(critical separation between static and dynamic context.) Tj T*
(Static context is always loaded: system instructions, rule files \(AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md,) Tj T*
(GEMINI.md\), global memory, and persona definitions. It defines who the agent is and how) Tj T*
(it behaves. Static context is expensive because every token is present in every interaction,) Tj T*
(regardless of relevance.) Tj T*
(Dynamic context is loaded on demand: skill instructions triggered by task matching, tool) Tj T*
(results retrieved during execution, documents fetched from RAG pipelines, and windowed) Tj T*
(session history. Dynamic context is efficient because the agent pays the token cost only) Tj T*
(when the information is needed.) Tj T*
(The design decision of what belongs in static context versus dynamic context is a genuine) Tj T*
(engineering trade-off. Too much static context wastes tokens and dilutes signals. Too little) Tj T*
(means the agent forgets critical rules. The best systems treat this boundary as a first-class) Tj T*
(architectural decision, reviewed and versioned like any other configuration.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
