(Page 18 of 51 - 02 - The New SDLC  With Vibe Coding) Tj T*
(The new SDLC with vibe coding) Tj T*
(May 2026) Tj T*
(18) Tj T*
(Agent Skills have seen rapid adoption across major coding agents and enterprise platforms) Tj T*
(because they solve four problems that have plagued AI agent development:) Tj T*
(* Context rot from overloaded prompts) Tj T*
(* Absence of procedural memory for LLMs) Tj T*
(* Operational overhead of multi-agent architectures) Tj T*
(* Need for portability across tools and vendors) Tj T*
(This section introduced the core principles of context engineering: the six types of context) Tj T*
(every agent needs, the trade-off between static and dynamic context, and Agent Skills as the) Tj T*
(key pattern for managing that trade-off at scale.) Tj T*
(The companion Day-3 paper in this series on Context Engineering: Sessions, Skills & Memory) Tj T*
(takes each of these ideas further, covering how to design and manage sessions, write and) Tj T*
(evaluate skills, build persistent memory across interactions, and optimize token economics) Tj T*
(for production systems.) Tj T*
(The shift from "prompt engineering" to "context engineering" reflects a deeper truth about) Tj T*
(working with AI. Models don't need cleverly worded instructions as much as they need the) Tj T*
(same context that a skilled human developer would need to do good work. The question) Tj T*
(isn't "how do I trick the AI into writing good code?" It's "what would a new team member) Tj T*
(need to know to contribute effectively, and how do I encode that knowledge in a form the AI) Tj T*
(can use?") Tj T*
(Context engineering is the bridge between vibe coding and agentic engineering. It is also the) Tj T*
(bridge between this section and the next one, where we look at the structure that surrounds) Tj T*
(every model and makes it useful.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
