(19) Tj T*
(By shifting our focus from writing syntax to engineering this context, the bottlenecks in) Tj T*
(software creation fundamentally change. We are no longer waiting on human hands to type) Tj T*
(boilerplate; we are waiting on human minds to define the boundaries. This necessitates a) Tj T*
(complete reimagining of the traditional Software Development Life Cycle \(SDLC\), as the) Tj T*
(systems we use to build software now dictate the speed at which it is delivered.") Tj T*
(The new software development life cycle) Tj T*
(The traditional SDLC under pressure) Tj T*
(The software development life cycle has already been through one major transformation.) Tj T*
(Over the past two decades, most enterprises moved from sequential waterfall processes to) Tj T*
(iterative models: Agile sprints, continuous integration, DevOps pipelines, and rapid release) Tj T*
(cycles. That shift shortened feedback loops, brought testing closer to development, and) Tj T*
(made deployment a continuous process rather than a quarterly event.) Tj T*
(AI compresses this cycle dramatically, but unevenly: implementation that once took weeks) Tj T*
(can now be done in hours, while requirements, architecture, and verification remain) Tj T*
(stubbornly human-paced. The result is not a faster version of the old SDLC. It is a different) Tj T*
(workflow, where the boundaries between phases blur, iteration cycles shorten from weeks) Tj T*
(to minutes, and the developer's role shifts from primary implementor to system designer and) Tj T*
(quality arbiter.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
