(The new SDLC with vibe coding) Tj T*
(May 2026) Tj T*
(22) Tj T*
(AI excels at implementing architectural decisions once they are made. Given a clear) Tj T*
(architecture document, AI agents can scaffold entire applications, generate consistent) Tj T*
(patterns across modules, and ensure that new code conforms to established conventions.) Tj T*
(The developer's role shifts from writing boilerplate to making and documenting the structural) Tj T*
(decisions that boilerplate implements.) Tj T*
(Implementation) Tj T*
(Modern coding agents can generate entire features from natural-language descriptions,) Tj T*
(implement complex algorithms, and produce multi-file changes that work together correctly.) Tj T*
(The productivity gains are real: industry surveys report 25 to 39% productivity improvements,) Tj T*
(with some tasks seeing larger gains.?) Tj T*
(The picture is more nuanced than headline numbers suggest. A study by METR found that) Tj T*
(experienced developers using AI assistants actually took 19% longer on certain tasks, largely) Tj T*
(because of the time spent verifying, debugging, and correcting AI output.? AI does not) Tj T*
(eliminate implementation work so much as transform it from writing to reviewing, guiding,) Tj T*
(and verifying.) Tj T*
(Testing and quality assurance) Tj T*
(Testing AI-generated code requires evaluating not just what the agent produced, but how) Tj T*
(it got there. Output evaluation checks the final artifact: does the code compile, do the tests) Tj T*
(pass? Trajectory evaluation checks the full sequence of tool calls and intermediate reasoning.) Tj T*
(Both are necessary because a fluent output that skipped its verification steps is a more) Tj T*
(dangerous failure than one with a visible error.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
