(24) Tj T*
(Maintenance and evolution) Tj T*
(Perhaps the most underestimated transformation is in maintenance. Legacy codebases) Tj T*
(that were once impenetrable to new team members can now be navigated, understood,) Tj T*
(and modified with AI assistance. An AI agent can read a codebase, understand its patterns,) Tj T*
(identify the relevant files for a change, and implement modifications while respecting the) Tj T*
(existing architecture.) Tj T*
(This has significant implications for technical debt. Code that was considered "too risky) Tj T*
(to touch" because only its original authors understood it can now be safely refactored,) Tj T*
(modernized, and extended. AI agents can systematically migrate codebases between) Tj T*
(frameworks, update deprecated APIs, and modernize test suites - tasks that were previously) Tj T*
(so tedious and risky that they simply never happened.) Tj T*
(The factory model: building the system that builds software) Tj T*
(The mental model that ties these transformations together is what we call the factory model.) Tj T*
(In this model, the developer's primary output is not code - it's the system that produces) Tj T*
(code. This system includes:8) Tj T*
(* Specifications and context that define what needs to be built) Tj T*
(* Agents that translate specifications into implementation) Tj T*
(* Tests and quality gates that verify correctness) Tj T*
(* Feedback loops that route failures back to agents for correction) Tj T*
(* Guardrails that constrain agents to safe, predictable behavior) Tj T*
ET
endstream
