(The new SDLC with vibe coding) Tj T*
(May 2026) Tj T*
(28) Tj T*
(What's in the harness) Tj T*
(Concretely, a harness includes:) Tj T*
(* Instructions and Rule Files: The text that defines who the agent is, what it cares about,) Tj T*
(and what it is forbidden from doing. This includes AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, GEMINI.md,) Tj T*
(skill files, and sub-agent prompts.) Tj T*
(* Tools: The functions, MCP servers, and APIs the agent can call, plus the prose around) Tj T*
(them that tells the model when and how to call them.) Tj T*
(* Sandboxes and execution environments: Where the agent's code actually runs, what it) Tj T*
(has access to, what it cannot reach.) Tj T*
(* Orchestration logic: Sub-agent spawning, model routing, hand-offs between specialists,) Tj T*
(and the rules that govern when each one fires.) Tj T*
(* Guardrails or Hooks: Deterministic code that runs at specific lifecycle points: before a) Tj T*
(tool call, after a file edit, before a commit. Hooks are the place for things the agent should) Tj T*
(never forget but often does.) Tj T*
(* Observability: Logs, traces, evaluations, cost and latency metering. Without) Tj T*
(observability, there is no way to tell whether the agent is doing well or quietly drifting.) Tj T*
(If that sounds like a lot of surface area, it is. And it is the team's surface area, not the) Tj T*
(model provider's.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
