(Page 31 of 51 - 02 - The New SDLC  With Vibe Coding) Tj T*
(The new SDLC with vibe coding) Tj T*
(May 2026) Tj T*
(31) Tj T*
(The transition from 'vibe coding' to 'agentic engineering' is not simply about the tools you) Tj T*
(use--a developer can vibe code or apply agentic engineering using the exact same agent.) Tj T*
(Instead, it is defined by how deliberately you configure and apply the harness. Vibe coding) Tj T*
(relies on minimal or implicit scaffolding aimed purely at rapid implementation. Agentic) Tj T*
(engineering relies on clear, extensive harness abstractions that guide the AI from the very) Tj T*
(first planning document all the way through to production monitoring.) Tj T*
(The impact of this deliberate configuration is highly measurable. Public benchmarks make the) Tj T*
(size of the harness effect concrete. On Terminal Bench 2.0, one team moved a coding agent) Tj T*
(from outside the Top 30 to the Top 5 by changing only the harness, with no model change at) Tj T*
(all. A separate study at LangChain raised a coding agent's score on the same benchmark by) Tj T*
(13.7 points by tweaking only the system prompt, tools, and middleware around a fixed model.) Tj T*
(The everyday version of this observation is crucial for teams adopting AI across the SDLC:) Tj T*
(when an agent does something wrong, the first instinct is to blame the model. More often,) Tj T*
(the failure traces back to a missing tool, a vague rule, an absent guardrail, or a context) Tj T*
(window stuffed with noise. Most agent failures, examined honestly, are configuration failures.) Tj T*
(The developer's evolving role:) Tj T*
(conductors and orchestrators) Tj T*
(As AI takes over more of the implementation work, the developer's role is transforming in) Tj T*
(ways that are both exciting and disorienting. We find it useful to think of two modes that) Tj T*
(developers move between fluidly: conductor and orchestrator.12) Tj T*
ET
endstream
