(Page 34 of 51 - 02 - The New SDLC  With Vibe Coding) Tj T*
(The new SDLC with vibe coding) Tj T*
(May 2026) Tj T*
(34) Tj T*
(* Decomposition: Breaking large tasks into appropriately sized units for agent execution) Tj T*
(* Evaluation: Quickly assessing whether agent output meets quality standards) Tj T*
(* System design: Designing the constraints, tests, and feedback loops that keep) Tj T*
(agents productive) Tj T*
(The 80% problem) Tj T*
(A persistent challenge in AI-assisted development is what we call the 80% problem: AI agents) Tj T*
(can rapidly generate approximately 80% of the code for a feature, but the remaining 20%) Tj T*
(- the edge cases, error handling, integration points, and subtle correctness requirements -) Tj T*
(demands deep contextual knowledge that current models often lack.14) Tj T*
(The nature of AI errors has evolved from simple syntax mistakes to more insidious conceptual) Tj T*
(failures: wrong assumptions about business logic, failure to seek clarification on ambiguous) Tj T*
(requirements, missing edge cases, and architectural decisions that create subtle long-term) Tj T*
(maintenance burdens. These errors are harder to detect precisely because the code "looks) Tj T*
(right" and may even pass basic tests.) Tj T*
(The developers who navigate this challenge most effectively adopt a specific posture: they) Tj T*
(use AI for what it's good at \(rapid implementation of well-specified tasks\) while reserving) Tj T*
(their own attention for what AI struggles with \(ambiguous requirements, architectural trade-) Tj T*
(offs, and correctness verification\). They don't try to be faster by accepting everything the AI) Tj T*
(produces. They try to be faster by focusing their expertise where it matters most.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
