(Figure 9: The Economics of AI Development) Tj T*
(The Hidden Debt of Vibe Coding \(Low CapEx, High OpEx\)) Tj T*
(At first glance, vibe coding appears incredibly cost-effective. The barrier to entry is) Tj T*
(essentially zero: a standard monthly subscription to an AI assistant and a few casual prompts.) Tj T*
(The CapEx is negligible because the developer relies entirely on the model's baseline) Tj T*
(capabilities rather than investing time in system design.) Tj T*
(However, the economics of vibe coding hide a massive, compounding OpEx burden:) Tj T*
(* The Token Burn Rate: Every interaction with a Large Language Model \(LLM\) incurs a) Tj T*
(cost based on input and output tokens. In vibe coding, developers often dump massive,) Tj T*
(unstructured files into the context window and repeatedly ask the model to fix its own) Tj T*
(unverified mistakes. This creates an expensive "prompting loop" that burns through API) Tj T*
(tokens with low first-pass success rates.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
