(41) Tj T*
(* Maintenance Tax: Code written through ad-hoc prompting often lacks structural) Tj T*
(consistency. When a bug arises six months later, human engineers must spend days) Tj T*
(reverse-engineering unstructured, AI-generated "spaghetti" code.) Tj T*
(* Security Remediation: Without an automated evaluation harness, the rapid generation) Tj T*
(of code leads to the rapid generation of vulnerabilities. The cost of fixing a security flaw in) Tj T*
(production is exponentially higher than catching it during the design phase.) Tj T*
(The Investment of Agentic Engineering \(High CapEx,) Tj T*
(Low OpEx\)) Tj T*
(Agentic engineering flips this economic model. It requires a deliberate, upfront investment of) Tj T*
(engineering time and resources before a single line of production code is generated.) Tj T*
(The CapEx in agentic engineering includes designing API schemas, building deterministic) Tj T*
(test suites, and, most importantly, structuring the agent's context. While this upfront cost) Tj T*
(is higher, the marginal cost of shipping and maintaining a feature drops dramatically. The AI) Tj T*
(operates within a strictly governed "factory," meaning its output is structurally sound, pre-) Tj T*
(tested, and aligned with company standards.) Tj T*
(Context Engineering as a Financial Lever) Tj T*
(In the token economy, context engineering is not just a technical skill--it is a financial) Tj T*
(strategy. LLMs charge for every piece of information you send them. Passing an entire) Tj T*
(100,000-token repository into every prompt is financially unviable at scale.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
