(May 2026) Tj T*
(47) Tj T*
(Conclusion: Intent as the new Interface) Tj T*
(The transition from syntax to intent is not a future prediction - it's a present reality.) Tj T*
(Developers are already spending more time describing what they want than specifying how) Tj T*
(to build it. The SDLC is already being compressed, restructured, and reimagined around AI) Tj T*
(capabilities. The question is not whether this transformation will happen, but how effectively) Tj T*
(individual developers, teams, and organizations will navigate it.) Tj T*
(The framework we've presented in this paper - the spectrum from vibe coding to agentic) Tj T*
(engineering, the conductor-to-orchestrator model of developer roles, the taxonomy of) Tj T*
(ambient, workflow, and autonomous agents, and the factory model of software production) Tj T*
(- provides a set of mental models for making sense of a rapidly evolving landscape. These) Tj T*
(models will remain useful even as the specific tools and capabilities evolve.) Tj T*
(Three principles stand out as durable:) Tj T*
(1. Structure scales, vibes don't. Vibe coding is a valid approach for exploration,) Tj T*
(prototyping, and personal projects. But for software that organizations depend on, the) Tj T*
(discipline of agentic engineering - specifications, tests, guardrails, and human oversight) Tj T*
(of architecture - is not optional. The gap between "it seems to work" and "it works) Tj T*
(correctly under all conditions" is where production outages, security vulnerabilities, and) Tj T*
(maintenance nightmares live.) Tj T*
(2. AI amplifies your engineering culture. Organizations with strong testing practices, clear) Tj T*
(architectural standards, and healthy code review processes get dramatically more value) Tj T*
(from AI-assisted development than those without. AI is a force multiplier - and it multiplies) Tj T*
(both your strengths and your weaknesses.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
